The error log indicates a "buffer overflow detected" during the `test_details` test case.
Upon reviewing the `src/main.c` file, the `struct details_entries` is defined with a `char expected_name[4]` field.

```c
struct details_entries {
	char expected_name[4];
	uint8_t expected_handlers;
	bool expected_test;

	bool matched_name;
	bool matched_handlers;
	bool matched_test;
};
```

However, the test code attempts to copy longer strings into this field using `strcpy`:
- `OS_MGMT_NAME` is "os mgmt" (7 characters + null terminator = 8 bytes).
- `ENUM_MGMT_NAME` is "enum mgmt" (9 characters + null terminator = 10 bytes).
- `SHELL_MGMT_NAME` is "shell mgmt" (10 characters + null terminator = 11 bytes).

All of these strings are longer than the allocated `4` bytes for `expected_name`, leading to a buffer overflow when `strcpy` is called. The longest string is "shell mgmt", which requires 10 characters plus a null terminator, totaling 11 bytes.

To fix this, the `expected_name` array size needs to be increased to at least 11.

```c
tests/subsys/mgmt/mcumgr/enum_mgmt/src/main.c
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
struct details_entries {
	char expected_name[4];
	uint8_t expected_handlers;
	bool expected_test;
========
struct details_entries {
	char expected_name[11]; /* Max length of "shell mgmt" (10) + null terminator */
	uint8_t expected_handlers;
	bool expected_test;
>>>>>>>> REPLACE
```
